{
  "_comment": "HANDLE RARITY grade for scripts/webpivot/pivot_suggest.py :: handle_rarity — the string-only half of techniques/username-osint.md §7.2 (an adaptation of Perito et al., PETS 2011: a handle built from common tokens is shared by many unrelated people, so reusing it says little). The grade sets how hard pivot_suggest pushes a username_reuse / username_variant pivot; it is a PIVOT PRIORITY, never a linkage or identity score. A RARE handle is a lead toward 'same controller' (claim ladder L2), still not L2. Brand/platform plus generic-part handles, public-figure names and keyboard walks are GENERIC. The grade still cannot detect deliberate copying of a distinctive handle, squatting or bulk generation, and does not run the population check (§7.2 step 3) — the analyst does. Tuning direction: ADDING a common token or pattern makes the tool MORE conservative (more handles graded GENERIC); removing one manufactures stronger leads.",
  "grades": {
    "_comment": "Per grade: priority_cap = the highest priority a username pivot may carry; confidence_scale multiplies the rule's base confidence (exact reuse 0.9, cross-platform variant 0.85, same-platform variant 0.65). GENERIC carries no linkage weight per username-osint §7.2, so it is capped at low.",
    "rare": {"priority_cap": "high", "confidence_scale": 1.0},
    "moderate": {"priority_cap": "medium", "confidence_scale": 0.7},
    "generic": {"priority_cap": "low", "confidence_scale": 0.2}
  },
  "limits": {
    "_comment": "short_max_len: a normalised base this short is GENERIC. rare_min_len + rare_min_unknown_run: RARE needs a base at least this long containing an uncommon run at least this long. max_generic_digit_suffix: name/word + up to this many trailing digits stays GENERIC (P14: trailing digits often look like a birth year — a lead, not a DOB). min_token_len: shorter vocabulary entries are ignored when segmenting (two-letter tokens cover random strings too easily). keyboard_walk_min_run: a run of at least this many characters read along one keyboard_walks sequence (either direction) counts as a walk; keyboard_walk_min_share: a handle whose separator-stripped string is at least this share walk runs is GENERIC.",
    "short_max_len": 4,
    "rare_min_len": 8,
    "rare_min_unknown_run": 4,
    "max_generic_digit_suffix": 4,
    "min_token_len": 3,
    "keyboard_walk_min_run": 4,
    "keyboard_walk_min_share": 0.6
  },
  "platform_default_patterns": {
    "_comment": "Regexes (Python re, matched against the lower-cased raw handle) for platform-assigned or placeholder handles. A match is GENERIC: the platform, not the person, chose the string.",
    "values": [
      "^(user|guest|member|player|account|id|fb|tiktok|tg|anon|anonymous|unknown|default|test)[_.-]?\\d{3,}$",
      "^\\d+$",
      "^[a-z]{1,3}\\d{6,}$",
      "^[a-z]+[_.-]?[0-9a-f]{8,}$",
      "^[0-9a-f]{10,}$"
    ]
  },
